  "caption": "H-soft concentrates near-positive samples across the fixed AB-blocked folds. With 20 selections per fold (100 total), it yields 68 hits and mean EF=62.1024, versus 10, 1 and 0 hits for additive Ridge, mean and the fixed random realization. The event is V<=2; hits are summed and EF is averaged equally over the five folds. Budget axes are logarithmic. The inset enlarges mean/random EF on the same k scale. The EF=1 line is the uniform-random expectation, not the observed random curve. The table reports every fold-specific N, M, h and existing unadjusted hypergeometric p value at k=20. These p values are descriptive uniform-null references after development selection, not a pooled or selection-adjusted significance test.",
